From: Paul Levickij <plevickij57@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp4: vote scanout memory bandwidth

MDP4 currently enables its AXI clock but never requests interconnect
bandwidth.  That leaves the MSM8x60 MMSS and APPSS fabric arbitration
entries at zero and causes a primary-interface underrun on every frame.

Acquire the optional mdp0-mem path and keep a conservative scanout vote
active.  The values are the default EBI framebuffer vote from the Sony
MSM8x60 board support: 407808000 bytes/s average and 1019520000 bytes/s
peak.  Platforms without an interconnect description continue to work as
before.

Describe the optional path in the MDP4 binding as well.

Signed-off-by: Paul Levickij <plevickij57@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/display/msm/mdp4.yaml | 10 ++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp4/mdp4_kms.c      | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/mdp4.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/mdp4.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/mdp4.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/msm/mdp4.yaml
@@ -46,6 +46,16 @@ properties:
   iommus:
     maxItems: 4
 
+  interconnects:
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 2
+
+  interconnect-names:
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - const: mdp0-mem
+      - const: mdp1-mem
+
   ports:
     $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/properties/ports
     properties:
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp4/mdp4_kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp4/mdp4_kms.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp4/mdp4_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp4/mdp4_kms.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/interconnect.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_bridge.h>
 #include <drm/drm_bridge_connector.h>
@@ -532,11 +533,39 @@ static const struct dev_pm_ops mdp4_pm_ops = {
 	.complete = msm_kms_pm_complete,
 };
 
+static int mdp4_setup_interconnect(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct icc_path *path;
+	int ret;
+
+	path = devm_of_icc_get(dev, "mdp0-mem");
+	if (IS_ERR(path))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(path),
+				     "failed to get MDP memory path\n");
+	if (!path)
+		return 0;
+
+	/* Sony's default MSM8x60 EBI framebuffer vote. */
+	ret = icc_set_bw(path, Bps_to_icc(407808000),
+			 Bps_to_icc(1019520000));
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "failed to vote MDP memory bandwidth\n");
+
+	dev_info(dev, "MDP memory vote: 407808000/1019520000 Bps\n");
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int mdp4_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct mdp4_kms *mdp4_kms;
-	int irq;
+	int irq, ret;
+
+	ret = mdp4_setup_interconnect(pdev);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	mdp4_kms = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*mdp4_kms), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!mdp4_kms)
-- 
2.51.0
